; Minimal probe for stringContains (contract entry 37): one node, five needle
; shapes. `testDiffStdlib` already calls `contains` once, but buried behind two
; `stringCase` calls, so it could not be attributed.
;
; ASCII-only, for the same structural reason as `testDiffStringCase`: the
; contract's reading is grapheme-wise, the LLVM emitter's is a `strstr` byte
; search, and the two part company only under decomposed or multi-scalar
; Unicode -- which this harness cannot host, because it asserts the channels
; agree.
;
; The empty needle is called out because the two readings have to agree about
; it as well: `StdlibPini` returns true before searching, and `strstr` also
; matches an empty needle at offset 0. An empty receiver is here to pin that
; the answer is false rather than an error.

main|func() -> ():
    var s = "Hello, World"
    print(s.contains("World"))
    print(s.contains("world"))
    print(s.contains(""))
    print(s.contains("Hello, World"))
    print(s.contains("Hello, World!"))
    print(s.contains("lo, W"))
    print("".contains(""))
    print("".contains("x"))
    return
